WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:22.173
Early one frosty January morning, the captain walked to the beach with his cutlass—the sword he always kept by his side—swinging under his old blue coat.

2
00:00:22.174 --> 00:00:28.668
He carried his brass telescope under his arm, and he had his hat tilted back on his head.

3
00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:33.255
The old man's breath hung in the air like smoke.

4
00:00:33.256 --> 00:00:35.924
Mother was helping my sick father upstairs,

5
00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:44.140
and I was setting the table for the captain's breakfast when the door opened and a pale, greasy-looking creature walked in.

6
00:00:44.141 --> 00:00:51.697
He was missing two fingers from his left hand and he wore a cutlass too, but he didn't look like a seafaring man.

7
00:00:51.698 --> 00:00:54.941
"May I help you, sir?" I asked.

8
00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:58.602
"I'll have some rum," he said.

9
00:00:58.603 --> 00:01:02.931
"Are you setting that table for my mate Bill?"

10
00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:06.360
"It's for the captain," I said.

11
00:01:06.361 --> 00:01:13.027
"Well," he said, "I expect Bill might like to be called 'captain.'

12
00:01:13.028 --> 00:01:19.779
Does your captain have a scar on one cheek and a pleasant personality when he's drunk?

13
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:25.801
Has he a sea chest that he guards most carefully?" I nodded.

14
00:01:25.802 --> 00:01:32.570
"Now, my lad, tell me, is my mate Bill here?"

15
00:01:32.571 --> 00:01:37.432
"He's out walking," I said. "He'll return soon."

16
00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:41.363
"Ah," said he, "good."

17
00:01:41.364 --> 00:01:47.405
The stranger hung around the door like a cat waiting for a mouse.

18
00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:54.754
Once, when I stepped outside, a change came over his face and he angrily said, "Get back in here!"

19
00:01:54.755 --> 00:02:00.846
Then he suddenly became very polite, half smiling and half sneering.

20
00:02:00.847 --> 00:02:08.469
"You're a good boy." He patted my shoulder. "I have a son of my own."

21
00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:15.994
Then the stranger looked out the window and said cheerfully, "Ah, here comes my friend Bill.

22
00:02:15.995 --> 00:02:23.995
Let's move aside, sonny, and we'll give Bill a little surprise—bless his heart."

23
00:02:23.996 --> 00:02:28.515
He pushed me back until we were both hidden behind the open door.

24
00:02:28.516 --> 00:02:32.340
I was very alarmed, but the stranger seemed frightened too.

25
00:02:32.341 --> 00:02:37.608
He swallowed hard and grabbed the handle of his cutlass, loosening the blade in its sheath.

26
00:02:37.609 --> 00:02:44.611
Unsuspecting, the captain marched in the door and across the room to the table where his breakfast lay.

27
00:02:44.612 --> 00:02:48.857
"Bill," the stranger said in a bold voice as he pushed me away.

28
00:02:48.858 --> 00:02:54.694
The captain spun around, and he became so pale that his nose was nearly blue.

29
00:02:54.695 --> 00:02:59.131
I felt sorry to see him suddenly turn so old and sick.

30
00:02:59.132 --> 00:03:04.999
"Black Dog!" gasped the captain, looking as if he'd seen a ghost.

31
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.761
"And who else?" the stranger said.

32
00:03:08.762 --> 00:03:17.668
"I'm here to see you, Billy, my old shipmate. It's been a while since I lost these two fingers."

33
00:03:17.669 --> 00:03:20.132
He held up his mutilated hand.

34
00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:27.994
"Well, you found me," the captain said, recovering. "Here I am. What do you want?"

35
00:03:27.995 --> 00:03:36.192
"Let's just sit down over there and talk like old shipmates, Billy Bones," Black Dog said.

36
00:03:36.193 --> 00:03:40.971
Then Black Dog looked at me. "Leave us.

37
00:03:40.972 --> 00:03:46.944
And I don't want to see you listening to our conversation, sonny."

38
00:03:46.945 --> 00:03:53.014
I left them at the table, but I did my best to pick up a word or two from where I waited at the bar.

39
00:03:53.015 --> 00:03:55.652
I heard mostly curses from the captain.

40
00:03:55.653 --> 00:04:03.526
"No, no, no!" he cried. "If I'm going to hang, then everyone will!"

41
00:04:03.527 --> 00:04:08.394
They shouted and swore and began to fight, knocking over a chair and table.

42
00:04:08.395 --> 00:04:11.707
I ran over to watch as their cutlasses clashed.

43
00:04:11.708 --> 00:04:15.447
Then Black Dog let out a cry of pain.

44
00:04:15.448 --> 00:04:19.021
He turned and started to run with the captain right behind him.

45
00:04:19.022 --> 00:04:24.676
Blood was streaming from Black Dog's left shoulder as he sprinted through the door.

46
00:04:24.677 --> 00:04:28.940
The captain took aim with his cutlass and threw it at Black Dog,

47
00:04:28.941 --> 00:04:35.932
and he might have split Black Dog's head in half if not for our big sign saying "Admiral Benbow."

48
00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:39.550
The frame still has a nick where the sword hit it.

49
00:04:39.551 --> 00:04:43.829
Despite his wound, Black Dog ran off and disappeared over the hill.

50
00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.677
The captain rubbed his eyes and went inside.

51
00:04:47.678 --> 00:04:52.725
"Jim," he said, clutching the wall, "I need some rum."

52
00:04:52.726 --> 00:04:54.849
"Are you hurt?" I cried.

53
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:59.089
"Rum," he repeated. "Rum! Rum!"

54
00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:05.375
Shaking, I ran to get it, but my hands were so unsteady I broke the glass and had to fill another.

55
00:05:05.376 --> 00:05:09.744
Suddenly, I heard a loud crash and ran toward the sound.

56
00:05:09.745 --> 00:05:12.849
The captain was lying on the floor.

57
00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.646
Alarmed by all the noise, Mother came downstairs.

58
00:05:16.647 --> 00:05:25.119
"He's drunk! What a disgrace!" she cried. "And with your poor father sick!"

59
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.935
My mother and I raised the captain's head.

60
00:05:27.936 --> 00:05:32.157
His eyes were closed and he was breathing loud and hard.

61
00:05:32.158 --> 00:05:36.616
I had the rum, but his teeth and jaws were shut tight.

62
00:05:36.617 --> 00:05:41.885
We were relieved when the door opened, and we saw Dr. Livesey, here to visit Father.

63
00:05:41.886 --> 00:05:45.152
"Oh, Doctor!" Mother cried.

64
00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:49.027
"He looks as if he's had a stroke," said the doctor.

65
00:05:49.028 --> 00:05:52.866
"Now, Mrs. Hawkins, run upstairs to your husband.

66
00:05:52.867 --> 00:05:57.162
I'll do my best to help this worthless fellow."

67
00:05:57.163 --> 00:06:02.136
The doctor had just loosened the captain's collar when the old man awoke.

68
00:06:02.137 --> 00:06:06.737
The captain recognized the doctor and frowned, and then he saw me.

69
00:06:06.738 --> 00:06:12.432
"Where's Black Dog?" he asked, trying to raise himself up.

70
00:06:12.433 --> 00:06:15.910
"There's no black dog here," said the doctor.

71
00:06:15.911 --> 00:06:18.580
"You drank too much and had a stroke."

72
00:06:18.581 --> 00:06:21.692
"Where is he?" the captain gasped.

73
00:06:21.693 --> 00:06:24.452
"Listen to me," the doctor said.

74
00:06:24.453 --> 00:06:32.322
"One drink won't kill you, but keep drinking one after another and you'll die—do you understand that?—die."

75
00:06:32.323 --> 00:06:35.839
We hoisted the captain upstairs and put him to bed.

76
00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:41.089
"Heed my words," said the doctor. "Rum will kill you."

77
00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:45.746
Out of earshot, the doctor told me, "He should rest for a week.

78
00:06:45.747 --> 00:06:52.849
Another stroke could end his sorry life."
